The area of a rectangle is given by length × width. Since the area is 360 square feet and the length is 9 feet, the width can be calculated as:  
Width = Area / Length = 360 / 9 = <<360/9=40>>40 feet.  

Now, calculate the perimeter (sum of all sides) in feet:  
